     <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPIUF supported community led infrastructure, human development and waste management initiatives in the Solomon Islands through additional financing of AUD11.7m to the World Bank for the Community Access and Urban Services Enhancement Project (CAUSE). Since commencing in 2018, CAUSE has trained and engaged 8,345 unemployed with equal representation of females (51%) and youth (51%) who worked on the delivery of 209 climate-resilient infrastructure projects (including Jacobs ladders, sidewalks, road maintenance and improvements to Honiara&#x2019;s Central Market) improving access to quality infrastructure, distributed SBD25.84m in wages supporting the community and vulnerable people, and collected over 64,138m3 of urban waste.</narrative>
