   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPIUF supported the World Bank correspondent banking relationships (CBR) project, digital ID infrastructure, and financial stability efforts across the Pacific. We supported the establishment of a feasibility study of a Pacific Payments Aggregation Mechanism to address a key cause of Pacific bank de-risking &#x2013; the scale of Pacific banking. We supported digital ID projects and business cases for digital ID infrastructure in seven jurisdictions (Federated States of Micronesia, Kiribati, Marshall Islands, Palau, Samoa, Tonga and Tuvalu) to improve ability of banks to meet global Anti-Money Laundering requirements and support financial inclusion. We also supported a Deposit Insurance Policy Paper on establishing a deposit insurance scheme in Fiji to drive improvements in financial stability.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
